# SPA history fallback.
#
# The app uses real paths (/app/live, /app/decisions), not hash routing, so a
# hard refresh or a pasted deep link asks the host for a file that does not
# exist. Without this rule Cloudflare Pages answers 404 and the user sees
# nothing — the one routing bug that only ever shows up in production.
#
# Status 200, not 301: the browser must keep the URL it asked for so the router
# can read it. A redirect would rewrite the address bar to "/" and lose the page.
# Real assets are served before this rule is consulted, so it does not shadow
# anything in /assets.
/*    /index.html   200
